DCE Security and the World Wide Web 

The OSF DCE User & Developer Conference being held April 16-
18, 1996, in San Jose, CA., is pleased to announce the addition of a 
new track to the conference program: DCE Security and the World 
Wide Web.

This track is intended for those who are utilizing the World Wide 
Web within their computing infrastructure. The World Wide Web 
is the fastest growing segment of the Internet. In order to be 
successful though, the Web must address issues such as security 
and scalable naming. Attendees learn how to combine the Web and 
DCE, with its global naming architecture and integrated security 
model, to address these issues and more.

Topics covered in this track include:

 - "Architecting for Enterprise Security," David Hemsath, IBM
 - "Networked Computer Security for DCE," Sean Leonard, 
Hewlett-Packard
 - "DCE and the Internet: User Applications and Technical Issues," 
Hal Lockhart, Locus Computing Corp.
 - "Single Sign-On and DCE," Thomas Klejna, OSF
 - "The DCE Web: Securing the Enterprise Web," Steve Lewontin, 
OSF

New and updated tracks at the OSF DCE User & Developer 
Conference include:

