Check the bgnice environment variable - it will make background jobs run at a 
nice value (which makes them a bit slower...) You can do this using
  set -o
to get a list of all settings; bgnice is turned on by default, really.
To get rid of it, use
  set +o bgnice
and to turn it on again, use
  set -o bgnice


Cheers,

JJ


