Hey,

This is what I normaly do when I wan't a new disc on my system.It's no
differance between a DEC disc or a NON DEC disc.

1.Make sure you see the device at the boot prompt.The command ">>> show
device" will  list your devices on the system.

2.Do you see the device when you boot the system?If not and you have
genvmunix in /.Boot the system as  follows">>> boot -fi genvmunix".

3.Remove the *rz5* in /dev.Rerun MAKEDEV command in /dev as follows.
cd /dev ; ./MAKEDEV rz5.

The devices has the major/minor as follows:
X-IT_SK14>ls -la *rz5*
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5120 jun 21  1995 rrz5a
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5121 jun 21  1995 rrz5b
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5122 jun 21  1995 rrz5c
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5123 jun 21  1995 rrz5d
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5124 jun 21  1995 rrz5e
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5125 jun 21  1995 rrz5f
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5126 jun 21  1995 rrz5g
crw-------   1 root     system     8,5127 jun 21  1995 rrz5h
brw-------   1 root     system     8,5120 jun 21  1995 rz5a
brw-------   1 root     system     8,5121 jun 21  1995 rz5b
brw-rw-rw-   1 root     system     8,5122 jun 21  1995 rz5c
brw-------   1 root     system     8,5123 jun 21  1995 rz5d
brw-------   1 root     system     8,5124 jun 21  1995 rz5e
brw-------   1 root     system     8,5125 jun 21  1995 rz5f
brw-------   1 root     system     8,5126 jun 21  1995 rz5g
brw-------   1 root     system     8,5127 jun 21  1995 rz5h

If you wan't to make the disc fully known by the system you can insert
information about the disc in /sys/data/cam_data.c.If I don't recall
wrong it's from this file the disc's gets it's default partition layout.

hope this will take you a little bit closer.

Regard's

/stefan



