In article <4duvrq$h5@noc.tor.hookup.net>, andyl@netinc.ca (Andy Leitzinger) writes:
|>Hi,
|>	I've got a DEC UNIX v3.2 alpha server. I also have the v3.2 CD. How do  
|>I find and install the MAN pages? 
|>
|>Thanks, Andy
|>

By using the "setld" command.  I'd tell you to read the manpage, but that
wouldn't be very helpful - would it?  Instead, try typing just setld and you'll
get its usage information.

If you have the V3.2 CD mounted at /mnt, you can issue the command:

setld -l /mnt/ALPHA/BASE

and you'll be presented with a menu of all the subsets which you have not yet
installed, including the man page subsets.  Pick what you want!

Dave



