But whoever sends mail to the user has to get the case right, and
mailers that don't preserve case in addresses (VMS) screw things up
royally. 

Downcase all the usernames. Its the only practical option, otherwise
you'll be chasing lost mail for users forever. If there's a clash ( same
name, different case ) you're gonna have to change one of them. 


All uppercase  login ids cause other problems of course - esp. the
helpful way so many unix's assume that if you type in an all-upper login
id, then you must have a teletype that isn't capable of lower case.

Probably
