Our site is running Digital UNIX 3.2A and the advfs.  Nightly backups 
are run in single user mode using vdump.  The verbose option of vdump 
is used to generate a log of files backuped.  Occasionally, when a 
backup is run using vdump, the error 'filesystemname: write failed, file 
system is full' is generated on whatever file system the logs are being 
written to.  

After the system is halted and booted to single user mode, the file 
systems can be mounted.   If you issue a df or a showfsets of the full 
domain, the file system appears full.  If you issue an 'ls -l' or a du 
on the suspect domain, the problem clears up and any further df or 
showfsets show the correct disk usage.  

If you can help or are having a similar problem, please post a reply or 
email me directly.  Any information would be appreciated.

Barbara Wilkey
Computing Resources
UT Health Science Center @ SA
wilkey@uthscsa.edu



